Package: mvImputer
Type: Package
Title: Multivariate Imputation of Mixed-Type Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Carl", "Brunius", email = "carl.brunius@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Imputes missing values in numeric and mixed-type tables
    (numeric, integer, factor, ordered, character and logical columns).
    Each column with gaps is predicted from all the others by an iterative
    random-forest or partial least squares model, by default in two stages,
    with a stopping rule scaled by the standard deviation of each numeric
    column. Results are reproducible for a given seed whatever the number
    of parallel workers. The caller's random-number state is restored on
    exit, except that the default seed = NULL takes one draw from it.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: future, future.apply, ranger, randomForest, stats, parallel, withr
Suggests: mixOmics, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Encoding: UTF-8
BugReports: https://github.com/CarlBrunius/mvImputer/issues
